  "situation": "South Africa was emerging from decades of conflict between a minority that controlled state institutions and a majority that resisted that domination. The interim Constitution committed the country to transition toward a more just and democratic order based on fundamental human rights. Its epilogue connected national unity and reconciliation with addressing past violations and directed Parliament to establish an amnesty framework. The framework under consideration could make amnesty conditional on full disclosure and a connection to political objectives in the past conflicts. Victims and their dependents faced a choice between seeking prosecution and punishment and pursuing a process intended to uncover what happened to their loved ones.",
